{
  "sourceNullable": "{\"cells\":[{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":\"# VQCC | R10 Merged-Group DF-THC Chemistry | LB 12.87\\n\\nPublic leaderboard **12.87220** for this exact submission. The chemistry (`dfthcsos`) is new:\\na **10-group, 129-vector, 60-copy DF-THC factorization at 8-bit angles** reaching **5.99x** the reference\\n(official cost 5.59893e8). The arithmetic (`invsqrt`) and `dqi` circuits are the public Apache-2.0 circuits from\\n[Artem1410 / anazemcev's THC Joint Norm + 881Q DQI](https://www.kaggle.com/code/anazemcev/quantum-circuits-thc-joint-norm-881q-dqi),\\nused unchanged and re-verified here.\\n\\n| task | circuit | Q | Toffoli / C | R / lambda_eff | official cost | ratio |\\n|:--|:--|--:|--:|--:|--:|--:|\\n| invsqrt | Phuc Thai EXP-225a (via Artem1410) | 82 | C = 1684.09 | - | 138,095.03 | 15.04x |\\n| dqi | paired-v6 decoder (Artem1410 / anazemcev) | 881 | 1,116,994 | R = 1.1913 | 1.03278e12 | 23.66x |\\n| dfthcsos | **this notebook: R10/B129/C60, brot 8** | 447 | 26,078 | lambda_eff 48.031 | 5.59893e8 | **5.99x** |\\n| geometric mean | | | | | | **12.87** |\\n\\nRun All rebuilds the 11 chemistry circuits from the factorization, runs **all three official verifiers in full**\\nand writes `submission.zip`.\\n\\n## Chemistry: how the factorization was made\\n\\nEverything is in the dataset [vqcc-dfthc-r10-merged-groups](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/michaelrustad/vqcc-dfthc-r10-merged-groups)\\n(training sources in `src/`, PyTorch/CUDA, run locally).\\n\\n1. **Merge groups.** Start from Ahmed Berat Ozer's public (26, 60, 30) factorization and merge pairs of groups into\\n   (13, 129, 60): each merged group holds its two parents exactly (block weights), so nothing is lost. At brot 8,\\n   B >= 129 lowers the inner QROAM block size, which cuts the temporary register from ~542 to ~304 qubits.\\n2. **Drop groups with long refits.** Drop the weakest group and refit the continuous factorization with L-BFGS\\n   (with the D(w) penalty), 13 -> 12 -> 11 -> 10 groups. L-BFGS refits reach much lower error than Adam\\n   (R10 continuous error_2 10.26 mHa).\\n3. **Progressive quantization** of the Givens angle words to 8 bits: 64 stages x 400 Adam steps; each stage freezes\\n   the least sensitive words at their rounded values and lets the rest compensate. More, shorter stages beat fewer,\\n   longer ones (19.56 vs 20.00 mHa for 32 x 600).\\n4. **Finish:** one-body (Wo) effective-norm refit and one-body flips, Gram-preserving column rotations, then a joint\\n   w / Wo lambda_eff descent under an error_2 cap of 19.85 mHa, then finish + rotations again.\\n   Final: error_2 19.65 mHa, lambda_eff 48.03.\\n5. **Circuits:** signed half-open Givens gauge (the top bit equals the next one, so 7 bits are loaded) and a\\n   2-address banked QROM, 7 words per ANGLE circuit: 11 circuits, 124 qubits each.\\n\\n## Credits\\n\\n* `invsqrt`: Phuc Thai's EXP-225a (Apache-2.0), packaged by Artem1410 / anazemcev; lineage Dmitrii Gluzdov,\\n  Sumit Chongder, anazemcev, Kozykorpesh, Zongao Bian.\\n* `dqi`: Artem1410 / anazemcev paired-v6 decoder (Apache-2.0), built on SomeJoint's in-place J-fraction decoder and the\\n  public DQI work it credits.\\n* Chemistry starting point: the public (65, 60, 30) DF-THC factorization and\\n  [Ahmed Berat Ozer's DF-THC Group Compression](https://www.kaggle.com/code/ahmedberatozer/quantum-ai-df-thc-group-compression)\\n  (26, 60, 30) factorization; `gauge_qrom` by Ahmed Berat Ozer; banked QROM / ANF eraser by Kozykorpesh, Sumit Chongder,\\n  Kirill Tymchishin and anazemcev (all Apache-2.0).\\n* Effective-norm refinement and gauge rotations follow the public chemistry refinement notebooks (reimplemented).\\n\\nNew code here is Apache-2.0.\"},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":\"import glob, hashlib, json, os, shutil, subprocess, sys, time, zipfile\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\ndef find_dir(name):\\n    hits = sorted(glob.glob(f'/kaggle/input/**/{name}', recursive=True), key=len)\\n    assert hits, f'attach input: {name}'\\n    return Path(hits[0])\\n\\nCOMP = find_dir('google-verifiable-quantum-circuit-compilation')\\nMINE = find_dir('vqcc-dfthc-r10-merged-groups')\\nVERIFIERS = COMP / 'verifiers'\\nos.environ['QCC_VERIFIERS'] = str(VERIFIERS)\\nsys.path[:0] = [str(COMP / 'kickmix'), str(VERIFIERS), str(MINE / 'src')]\\nimport kickmix as km\\nimport angles_qrom as AQ\\n\\nWORK = Path('/kaggle/working')\\nSUB = WORK / 'sub'\\nshutil.rmtree(SUB, ignore_errors=True)\\n(SUB / 'dfthcsos').mkdir(parents=True)\\n\\ndef sha256(p):\\n    h = hashlib.sha256()\\n    with open(p, 'rb') as f:\\n        for b in iter(lambda: f.read(1 << 22), b''):\\n            h.update(b)\\n    return h.hexdigest()\\n\\nprint('competition data:', COMP)\\nprint('factorization dataset:', MINE)\",\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":\"## invsqrt and dqi: public circuits, unchanged\\n\\nTaken from the output of the attached notebook `anazemcev/quantum-circuits-thc-joint-norm-881q-dqi`\\n(run of 2026-10-25). The SHA-256 values below are the bytes that scored 12.87220.\"},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":\"EXPECTED = {\\n    'invsqrt.kmb': '0f84f5bab3a02e6b357d4656553607174345a33d252cef643f9136db13212141',\\n    'dqi.kmb': '1161f7221de935ba1399ced409b9936d8b4cb570ef3314585d4b9bc2c5b24dd9',\\n}\\nzips = sorted(glob.glob('/kaggle/input/**/quantum-circuits-thc-joint-norm-881q-dqi/**/submission.zip', recursive=True))\\nassert zips, 'attach the notebook output anazemcev/quantum-circuits-thc-joint-norm-881q-dqi'\\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(zips[0]) as z:\\n    for name in EXPECTED:\\n        with z.open(name) as src, open(SUB / name, 'wb') as dst:\\n            shutil.copyfileobj(src, dst, 1 << 22)\\nfor name, want in EXPECTED.items():\\n    got = sha256(SUB / name)\\n    print(name, got, 'matches the 12.87 bytes' if got == want else 'DIFFERENT from the 12.87 bytes (upstream changed)')\",\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":\"## Chemistry: build the 11 ANGLE circuits\\n\\n`angles_qrom.canonical_words` re-encodes every decoded Givens vector in the signed half-open gauge; the words are\\nsplit into batches of J = 7 and each batch becomes one ANGLE_k circuit (2-address banked QROM).\"},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":\"FACT = MINE / 'fact' / 'dfthc_r10_b129_c60_brot8.npz'\\nprint('factorization sha256', sha256(FACT))\\nz = np.load(FACT, allow_pickle=False)\\nparams = {k: np.array(z[k]) for k in z.files}\\nbrot = int(params['brot'])\\nedges = params['tree_edges'].astype(np.int64)\\nwords = AQ.canonical_words(params['angle_words'], edges, brot)\\nJ = AQ.max_batch(brot, len(words), 2)\\nprint('(R, B, C) =', params['W'].shape, ' brot', brot, ' words', len(words), ' J', J)\\nt0 = time.time()\\nfor k, d in enumerate(AQ.batch_deltas(words, J)):\\n    c, rep = AQ.build2(d, brot, return_report=True)\\n    c.to_file(str(SUB / 'dfthcsos' / f'angle_k_{k}.kmb'), format='kmb')\\n    print(f'angle_k_{k}: {rep[\\\"num_qubits\\\"]} qubits, {rep[\\\"static_toffoli\\\"]} Toffoli')\\nnp.savez(SUB / 'dfthcsos' / 'submission.npz',\\n         **{k: params[k] for k in ('U', 'W', 'H2_I', 'H1_I', 'Hsym_lower', 'tree_edges')})\\nprint(f'built in {time.time() - t0:.0f} s')\",\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":\"## Official verifiers (full, default settings)\"},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":\"REF = {'invsqrt': 2076774.233715282, 'dqi': 24439463583672.93, 'dfthcsos': 3355599588.3155365}\\nenv = dict(os.environ, PYTHONPATH=os.pathsep.join([str(COMP / 'kickmix'), str(VERIFIERS)]))\\n\\ndef run_cli(module, path):\\n    t0 = time.time()\\n    p = subprocess.run([sys.executable, '-m', module, str(path)], cwd=VERIFIERS, env=env,\\n                       capture_output=True, text=True)\\n    out = p.stdout[p.stdout.index('{'):] if '{' in p.stdout else '{}'\\n    res = json.loads(out)\\n    print(module, res.get('status'), res.get('score'), f'{time.time() - t0:.0f} s')\\n    if res.get('status') != 'PASS':\\n        print(p.stdout[-3000:], p.stderr[-3000:])\\n    return res\\n\\nresults = {}\\nresults['invsqrt'] = run_cli('invsqrt.verify_submission_invsqrt', SUB / 'invsqrt.kmb')\\nresults['dqi'] = run_cli('dqi.verify_submission_dqi', SUB / 'dqi.kmb')\\nfrom dfthcsos.verify import verify as verify_chem\\nt0 = time.time()\\nresults['dfthcsos'] = verify_chem(str(SUB / 'dfthcsos'))\\nprint('dfthcsos', results['dfthcsos']['status'], results['dfthcsos']['score'], f'{time.time() - t0:.0f} s')\",\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":\"ratios = {t: REF[t] / results[t]['score'] for t in REF}\\nfor t, r in ratios.items():\\n    print(f'{t:9s} {results[t][\\\"status\\\"]:5s} cost {results[t][\\\"score\\\"]:.6e}  ratio {r:.4f}x')\\nassert all(results[t]['status'] == 'PASS' for t in REF)\\nscore = float(np.exp(np.mean(np.log(list(ratios.values())))))\\nprint(f'geometric mean: {score:.5f}')\\n\\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(WORK / 'submission.zip', 'w', zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED) as zf:\\n    for name in ('invsqrt.kmb', 'dqi.kmb'):\\n        zf.write(SUB / name, name)\\n    for p in sorted((SUB / 'dfthcsos').iterdir(), key=lambda p: (p.suffix != '.kmb', len(p.name), p.name)):\\n        zf.write(p, f'dfthcsos/{p.name}')\\n(WORK / 'results.json').write_text(json.dumps({'ratios': ratios, 'score': score, 'results': results},\\n                                              indent=1, default=str))\\nshutil.rmtree(SUB)\\nprint('wrote', WORK / 'submission.zip')\",\"execution_count\":null,\"outputs\":[]}],\"metadata\":{\"kernelspec\":{\"display_name\":\"Python 3\",\"language\":\"python\",\"name\":\"python3\"},\"language_info\":{\"name\":\"python\"}},\"nbformat\":4,\"nbformat_minor\":5}",
